    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="1098" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg998"/>

                <head>No. 634.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Farman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The dispatch of Mr. Comanos, numbered 340,
                    of the 8th of October last, respecting the proposed decree for insuring the
                    validity of the mortgage of certain lauds to the Messrs, Rothschild, has been
                    received. In reply to his request for instructions, I have to inform you that a
                    telegram upon the subject was sent on the 11th of October last, the text of
                    .which is as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Comanos</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul, Cairo, Egypt:</hi></p>
                        <p>This government makes no objection to the proposed decree respecting the
                            domanial loan.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
